The game ships two internal weapon bundles: <code>melee_weapon</code> and <code>range_weapon</code>. Internal base classes: <code>Weapon_Melee</code> and <code>Weapon_Range</code>, both derived from <code>Tool_Interacter</code>.

== Universal stats ==

Every weapon shares these stats (visible in the [[Template:Infobox weapon|infobox]] on each weapon page):

* '''Damage''': base damage per hit or per projectile
* '''Range''': melee reach or projectile max distance
* '''Fire rate''': attacks per second
* '''Durability''': hits before break; repairable at the matching workbench
* '''Ammo''' (ranged only): ammo type and magazine size

== Damage ==

All damage flows through a single method (<code>Battle_Info.MinusHP</code>). This means damage-modifier factors (see [[Perks]]) apply uniformly to all weapon types. See [[Combat]] for the full damage pipeline.

== Melee weapons ==

Melee is your baseline: no ammo, moderate damage, high stamina cost. Blades outperform blunt against unarmored zombies; blunt outperforms blades against armored / heavy variants. See [[Melee Weapons]].

== Ranged weapons ==

Ranged weapons trade ammo scarcity for range and safety. Bows are early-game craftable at [[Carpentry Workbench]]. Firearms are assembled at the [[Gun Workbench]] and require gunpowder (via the [[Biochemical Workbench]]).

Categories:

* '''Bows''': silent, wooden, common
* '''Crossbows''': higher damage, slower reload
* '''Firearms''': highest damage, loud (attracts zombies), gunpowder ammo

See [[Ranged Weapons]] and [[Ammunition]].

== Throwables ==

Throwables deal area damage and are consumed on throw.

== Repair ==

Every weapon has durability. Weapons at 0 durability become unusable but not destroyed. Return them to the matching workbench with the crafting material to repair.

